the biden administration is offering  temporary protection for ukrainian  refugees in the u.s letting them stay up  to 18 months the u.n says more than one  million refugees have fled ukraine in  just one week and that number is growing  fast chris lipsey is in la vie in  western ukraine which is the exit point  for many of those refugees  chris good morning  good morning the front line of the  conflict is out east while the front  line in the refugee crisis is out west  with the president of ukraine warning  vladimir putin wants to lower a new iron  curtain one that would hit the ground  right here  with each passing day of war more than  one hundred thousand ukrainian refugees  are added to the tally streaming into  neighboring countries moldova romania  slovakia hungary latvia and most of all  poland of the 1 million who have already  fled 500 000 of them are children the un  says and yet they are the lucky ones  roughly one million more people remain  internally displaced in a country  gripped by war such as these families at  a shelter in the western city of levive  the question on everyone's mind is  whether to stay in ukraine or to go  this grandmother and mother wish they  knew what was best for little alvina  only one year old  we have democracy says svetlana this is  our country not russia's we don't tell  russia how to live why should they tell  us  what is this conflict done to her future  [Music]  if our country is destroyed what can we  do i do not know she says  ukraine deprived ever more of its youth  and its innocence that's four-year-old  andre exhausted after 20 hours of  sleepless escape his father stayed  behind in their besieged city of harkiv  now it's just him his big brother and  their mom  we heard explosions over our heads at  the train station and all the way on the  train says olga you're aware you may  never return home every day begins with  a text to our relatives says 16 year old  dennis we ask are you alive  more than 2 000 civilians have been  killed ukraine says though the real cost  of war is always more than its death  toll and bravery is to be found beyond  the bullets and the front line  and just bear in mind the sad scenes  we're seeing here are even worse in  besieged cities like mariupol on the  coast where civilians are finding it  harder and harder if not impossible to  flee as russian forces surround them  gail  still so hard to comprehend thank you  very much chris livesay in la vie
 

